  $vtg$dragon-con-parade$vtg$, $vtg$atlanta$vtg$, $vtg$Dragon Con Parade$vtg$, $vtg$Costume parade / spectacle$vtg$, array[$vtg$Street$vtg$, $vtg$Portraits$vtg$]::text[], $vtg$Peachtree St, Downtown / Midtown$vtg$, 33.762, -84.386, null, $vtg$Saturday of Labor Day weekend, ~10am$vtg$, $vtg$2026-09-05T10:00$vtg$, $vtg$2026-09-05T13:00$vtg$, $vtg$high$vtg$, $vtg$free$vtg$, $vtg$free to watch — not ticketed$vtg$, $vtg$high$vtg$, $vtg$flat$vtg$, $vtg$Fifty thousand costumes marching down Peachtree$vtg$, $vtg$One of the country's best costume parades, free on the street$vtg$, $vtg$For a few hours Peachtree turns into the densest costume runway in the South — tens of thousands of elaborately built characters, in-character and happy to be photographed. It's a portrait shooter's fever dream and a street shooter's chaos, all in hard morning light against downtown's towers.$vtg$, array[$vtg$Hero portraits at the staging blocks before the march, where people hold still and pose$vtg$, $vtg$The parade in motion from a low angle, characters filling the frame against glass towers$vtg$, $vtg$Reaction shots in the crowd — kids, double-takes, phones up, the gap between costume and onlooker$vtg$]::text[], $vtg${"wide":"Get inside the march — a costumed figure filling the foreground, the column of characters and towers stretching behind","normal":"Work the staging area for eye-level, in-character portraits at a human distance","tele":"Pick a face out of the column from across the street — compress the costumes into a wall of color","macro":"Hunt the craft — armor rivets, prop detail, hand-stitched seams most people never notice"}$vtg$::jsonb, $vtg$Peachtree St between Peachtree Center and Civic Center MARTA; arrive early, streets close ~9:15am.$vtg$, $vtg$dragoncon.org/things-to-do/parade$vtg$, true)
