  $vtg$atlanta-dogwood-festival$vtg$, $vtg$atlanta$vtg$, $vtg$Atlanta Dogwood Festival$vtg$, $vtg$Arts festival$vtg$, array[$vtg$Street$vtg$, $vtg$Portraits$vtg$]::text[], $vtg$Piedmont Park, Midtown$vtg$, 33.7859, -84.3733, $vtg$piedmont$vtg$, $vtg$Second weekend of April$vtg$, $vtg$2027-04-09$vtg$, $vtg$2027-04-11$vtg$, $vtg$needs-date-verify$vtg$, $vtg$ticketed$vtg$, $vtg$FreshTix (own gate, ~$5/$10) — NOT Ticketmaster$vtg$, $vtg$high$vtg$, $vtg$golden$vtg$, $vtg$Ninety springs of artists under the dogwoods$vtg$, $vtg$Atlanta's oldest festival, the park in full bloom$vtg$, $vtg$One of the oldest arts festivals in the country, spread across Piedmont Park just as the dogwoods and azaleas peak. The draw for a photographer is the collision of blooming spring light, an artist market packed with texture, and a relaxed crowd that lingers — golden hour here is unusually generous with the Midtown skyline behind it.$vtg$, array[$vtg$The artist market tents backlit late in the day, color bleeding through the canvas$vtg$, $vtg$The crowd on the meadow with the Midtown skyline behind, golden hour raking across$vtg$, $vtg$Candid moments at the booths — makers talking with their hands, buyers deciding$vtg$]::text[], $vtg${"wide":"The meadow and skyline as one frame — festival sprawl foreground, Midtown towers behind at golden hour","normal":"Candid market life at a human distance — a maker mid-sentence, a buyer's face deciding","tele":"Compress a row of tents into stacked color, or lift a single face out of the crowd","macro":"The work itself — glaze on a pot, a brushstroke, petals on the ground"}$vtg$::jsonb, $vtg$Piedmont Park, Midtown; Midtown MARTA + a walk, or rideshare — parking is rough on festival weekend.$vtg$, $vtg$dogwood.org$vtg$, true)
