  $vtg$atlanta-jazz-festival$vtg$, $vtg$atlanta$vtg$, $vtg$Atlanta Jazz Festival$vtg$, $vtg$Music festival$vtg$, array[$vtg$Street$vtg$, $vtg$Portraits$vtg$]::text[], $vtg$Piedmont Park, Midtown$vtg$, 33.7859, -84.3733, $vtg$piedmont$vtg$, $vtg$Memorial Day weekend (late May)$vtg$, $vtg$2027-05-29$vtg$, $vtg$2027-05-31$vtg$, $vtg$needs-date-verify$vtg$, $vtg$free$vtg$, $vtg$free — one of the largest free jazz festivals in the country$vtg$, $vtg$high$vtg$, $vtg$golden$vtg$, $vtg$The whole city on a blanket, listening$vtg$, $vtg$Free jazz on the meadow, dusk light on the crowd$vtg$, $vtg$One of the largest free jazz festivals in the U.S. fills Piedmont's meadow for the long weekend — a wide, easy, all-ages crowd stretched out on blankets as the light goes gold and then blue behind the stage. It's less about the stage and more about the sea of people listening.$vtg$, array[$vtg$The blanket-covered meadow from a rise, bodies and skyline at golden hour$vtg$, $vtg$Stage-light spill on faces once blue hour sets in$vtg$, $vtg$Small human moments in the crowd — dancing, kids asleep, strangers sharing a spot$vtg$]::text[], $vtg${"wide":"The whole listening crowd as a landscape — meadow, stage, skyline in one sweep","normal":"Move through the blankets for intimate crowd candids at eye level","tele":"Isolate a face in the crowd lit by the stage, the rest melting to bokeh","macro":"The small stuff — a hand keeping time, a program, a shared plate"}$vtg$::jsonb, $vtg$Piedmont Park; Midtown MARTA + walk. Evenings are the shoot — plan for the light to fall.$vtg$, $vtg$atlantafestivals.com$vtg$, true)
