  $vtg$atlanta-pride-festival-parade$vtg$, $vtg$atlanta$vtg$, $vtg$Atlanta Pride Festival & Parade$vtg$, $vtg$Festival + parade$vtg$, array[$vtg$Street$vtg$, $vtg$Portraits$vtg$]::text[], $vtg$Piedmont Park + Peachtree St$vtg$, 33.7859, -84.3733, $vtg$piedmont$vtg$, $vtg$Second weekend of October (around National Coming Out Day)$vtg$, $vtg$2026-10-10$vtg$, $vtg$2026-10-11$vtg$, $vtg$high$vtg$, $vtg$free$vtg$, $vtg$free — festival in the park, parade down Peachtree$vtg$, $vtg$high$vtg$, $vtg$golden$vtg$, $vtg$The South's biggest Pride, color end to end$vtg$, $vtg$Parade down Peachtree, festival in the park$vtg$, $vtg$One of the largest Pride celebrations in the Southeast — a Sunday parade that pours down Peachtree from the Civic Center to Piedmont Park, then a two-day festival on the meadow. Relentless color, expression, and joy; nobody minds the camera.$vtg$, array[$vtg$The parade coming down Peachtree, marchers filling the avenue$vtg$, $vtg$Portraits at the park — people in full self-expression, holding still for you$vtg$, $vtg$Backlit flags and banners, color glowing through fabric in the afternoon sun$vtg$]::text[], $vtg${"wide":"The avenue packed curb to curb, a marcher in the foreground and the river of people behind","normal":"Consent-easy portraits in the park — people are here to be seen","tele":"Lift single expressions out of the parade from the curb","macro":"Detail and craft — pins, glitter, hand-lettered signs, painted faces"}$vtg$::jsonb, $vtg$Parade route runs Peachtree to Piedmont Park; Midtown MARTA drops you near the finish.$vtg$, $vtg$atlantapride.org$vtg$, true)
