  $vtg$sweet-auburn-springfest$vtg$, $vtg$atlanta$vtg$, $vtg$Sweet Auburn Springfest$vtg$, $vtg$Multicultural street festival$vtg$, array[$vtg$Street$vtg$, $vtg$Portraits$vtg$]::text[], $vtg$Sweet Auburn (Auburn Ave / JW Dobbs)$vtg$, 33.7554, -84.3742, $vtg$sweetauburn$vtg$, $vtg$Second weekend of May$vtg$, $vtg$2027-05-08$vtg$, $vtg$2027-05-09$vtg$, $vtg$needs-date-verify$vtg$, $vtg$free$vtg$, $vtg$free — one of the largest free street festivals in the Southeast$vtg$, $vtg$medium$vtg$, $vtg$golden$vtg$, $vtg$The historic heart of Black Atlanta, wide open$vtg$, $vtg$Huge free street festival on historic Auburn Ave$vtg$, $vtg$One of the largest free multicultural street festivals in the country takes over Auburn Avenue — the historic spine of Black Atlanta. Blocks of music stages, food, and vendors against the district's old storefronts, with a crowd that brings its whole self out.$vtg$, array[$vtg$The street packed end to end from a doorway or rise, storefronts framing the crowd$vtg$, $vtg$Vendor and food-stall candids — hands, steam, exchanges$vtg$, $vtg$Portraits against the historic Auburn Ave facades in late light$vtg$]::text[], $vtg${"wide":"Auburn Ave wall to wall — the historic storefronts and the full crowd in one frame","normal":"Street-level candids in the flow, the classic 35mm-in-the-crowd shot","tele":"Pull a face or a stall moment out of the density from up the block","macro":"Food and craft close up — a plate, a vendor's hands, a hand-painted sign"}$vtg$::jsonb, $vtg$Auburn Ave in Sweet Auburn; King Memorial MARTA is a short walk. Overlaps your Sweet Auburn spot.$vtg$, $vtg$sweetauburn.com$vtg$, true)
