  $vtg$candler-park-fall-fest$vtg$, $vtg$atlanta$vtg$, $vtg$Candler Park Fall Fest$vtg$, $vtg$Neighborhood festival$vtg$, array[$vtg$Street$vtg$, $vtg$Portraits$vtg$]::text[], $vtg$Candler Park$vtg$, 33.7676, -84.339, null, $vtg$First weekend of October$vtg$, $vtg$2026-10-03$vtg$, $vtg$2026-10-04$vtg$, $vtg$high$vtg$, $vtg$free$vtg$, $vtg$free — volunteer-run by the neighborhood$vtg$, $vtg$medium$vtg$, $vtg$golden$vtg$, $vtg$A whole neighborhood spills into its park$vtg$, $vtg$Free, homegrown, the park full of people$vtg$, $vtg$A beloved volunteer-run neighborhood festival — artist market, local bands, a tour of homes, a 5K — set in the green of Candler Park with the intown tree canopy turning. It's small enough to feel human and photogenic in an unforced, local way.$vtg$, array[$vtg$The market and stage crowd under the fall canopy, dappled light$vtg$, $vtg$Neighborhood texture — dogs, strollers, porches, the local-ness of it$vtg$, $vtg$Band and audience in the golden end of the afternoon$vtg$]::text[], $vtg${"wide":"The park and canopy holding the whole scene — market, crowd, autumn light","normal":"Warm neighborhood candids in the flow of the market","tele":"Compress the market rows, or catch a face mid-laugh across the field","macro":"Local details — a maker's booth, festival food, leaves underfoot"}$vtg$::jsonb, $vtg$Candler Park; Edgewood/Candler Park MARTA + a walk. Free and easygoing.$vtg$, $vtg$fallfest.candlerpark.org$vtg$, true)
