  $vtg$inman-park-festival$vtg$, $vtg$atlanta$vtg$, $vtg$Inman Park Festival$vtg$, $vtg$Street festival + parade$vtg$, array[$vtg$Street$vtg$, $vtg$Portraits$vtg$]::text[], $vtg$Inman Park$vtg$, 33.7592, -84.354, null, $vtg$Last weekend of April$vtg$, $vtg$2027-04-24$vtg$, $vtg$2027-04-25$vtg$, $vtg$needs-date-verify$vtg$, $vtg$free$vtg$, $vtg$free festival; parade is the centerpiece$vtg$, $vtg$medium$vtg$, $vtg$golden$vtg$, $vtg$Victorian porches and Atlanta's most eccentric parade$vtg$, $vtg$A gloriously weird parade through historic streets$vtg$, $vtg$Atlanta's oldest suburb throws a spring festival famous for one of the city's most eccentric, home-grown parades — winding past restored Victorian mansions and blooming gardens. Equal parts architecture, spring bloom, and delightful weirdness.$vtg$, array[$vtg$The parade winding under old trees past Victorian facades$vtg$, $vtg$Porch-and-garden vignettes as the festival spills through yards$vtg$, $vtg$Costumed marchers and hand-built floats at eye level$vtg$]::text[], $vtg${"wide":"A float or marcher framed by a blooming Victorian street","normal":"The parade at a human distance, characters and the crowd watching","tele":"Lift a single eccentric detail or face out of the procession","macro":"Spring bloom, costume craft, old-house detail"}$vtg$::jsonb, $vtg$Inman Park/Reynoldstown MARTA drops you at the edge; it's a walking festival.$vtg$, $vtg$inmanparkfestival.org$vtg$, true)
