  $vtg$little-five-points-halloween$vtg$, $vtg$atlanta$vtg$, $vtg$Little Five Points Halloween Festival & Parade$vtg$, $vtg$Costume parade / festival$vtg$, array[$vtg$Street$vtg$, $vtg$Portraits$vtg$]::text[], $vtg$Little Five Points$vtg$, 33.7648, -84.349, null, $vtg$Mid/late October (Sat–Sun); parade Sunday ~2pm$vtg$, $vtg$2026-10-17$vtg$, $vtg$2026-10-18$vtg$, $vtg$high$vtg$, $vtg$free$vtg$, $vtg$free to watch$vtg$, $vtg$medium$vtg$, $vtg$golden$vtg$, $vtg$Atlanta's weirdest neighborhood does Halloween right$vtg$, $vtg$A costume parade through the city's punk heart$vtg$, $vtg$Little Five Points — Atlanta's countercultural core — throws the city's best Halloween parade, an unhinged, creative, adults-lean-in spectacle through a neighborhood already covered in murals and character. If Dragon Con is polished cosplay, this is raw, homemade, and gloriously strange.$vtg$, array[$vtg$The parade coming through the L5P intersection, murals behind$vtg$, $vtg$Elaborate homemade costumes staged before the march$vtg$, $vtg$The crowd-and-costume overlap on the sidewalks, everyone in on it$vtg$]::text[], $vtg${"wide":"A costumed figure and the mural-covered street in one frame","normal":"Eye-level costume portraits in the staging crowd","tele":"Isolate a face or a grotesque detail from across the intersection","macro":"The homemade craft — makeup, prop rot, hand-built horror"}$vtg$::jsonb, $vtg$Euclid & Moreland, Little Five Points; rideshare or Inman Park MARTA + walk.$vtg$, $vtg$l5phalloween.com$vtg$, true)
