  $vtg$peachtree-road-race$vtg$, $vtg$atlanta$vtg$, $vtg$AJC Peachtree Road Race$vtg$, $vtg$10K road race$vtg$, array[$vtg$Street$vtg$, $vtg$Portraits$vtg$]::text[], $vtg$Peachtree St, Buckhead → Midtown$vtg$, 33.79, -84.383, null, $vtg$July 4, early morning$vtg$, $vtg$2027-07-04T06:30$vtg$, $vtg$2027-07-04T10:00$vtg$, $vtg$high$vtg$, $vtg$free to watch (runners register)$vtg$, $vtg$runners register via the race; free to spectate$vtg$, $vtg$high$vtg$, $vtg$flat$vtg$, $vtg$60,000 runners down Peachtree on the Fourth$vtg$, $vtg$The world's biggest 10K, a river of people$vtg$, $vtg$One of the largest 10K road races in the world sends 60,000 runners down Peachtree on July 4th morning — costumes, flags, hydrant spray, and an unbroken river of humanity in soft early light. A spectator's shoot, all energy and volume.$vtg$, array[$vtg$The mass of runners filling Peachtree from an overpass or rise$vtg$, $vtg$Costumed and flag-draped runners in the flow$vtg$, $vtg$Spectator-runner moments at the curb — hand-offs, hoses, high-fives$vtg$]::text[], $vtg${"wide":"The full river of runners down Peachtree, the avenue and crowd as scale","normal":"Curbside candids where runners and watchers meet","tele":"Compress the pack into a wall of bodies, or lift one costumed runner","macro":"The detail — bib numbers, flags, water spray frozen mid-air"}$vtg$::jsonb, $vtg$Peachtree St; the start is near Lenox/Buckhead MARTA, finish near Piedmont Park. Go early.$vtg$, $vtg$atlantatrackclub.org$vtg$, true)
