  $vtg$atlanta-caribbean-carnival$vtg$, $vtg$atlanta$vtg$, $vtg$Atlanta Caribbean Carnival$vtg$, $vtg$Cultural parade / festival$vtg$, array[$vtg$Street$vtg$, $vtg$Portraits$vtg$]::text[], $vtg$Central / Southwest Atlanta (route varies)$vtg$, 33.749, -84.388, null, $vtg$Late May (Saturday)$vtg$, $vtg$2027-05-29$vtg$, $vtg$2027-05-29$vtg$, $vtg$needs-date-verify$vtg$, $vtg$free to watch (some ticketed areas)$vtg$, $vtg$parade free; some fete/stage areas ticketed$vtg$, $vtg$medium$vtg$, $vtg$golden$vtg$, $vtg$Feathers, sequins, and soca down the avenue$vtg$, $vtg$Peak color — mas costumes in full sun$vtg$, $vtg$Atlanta's Caribbean Carnival brings a full mas parade — towering feathered-and-sequined costumes, soca trucks, and dancers — into hard, saturated daylight. Among the most purely colorful, high-energy shoots on the calendar, and the masqueraders want the camera.$vtg$, array[$vtg$Full mas costumes head-to-toe, feathers catching the sun$vtg$, $vtg$Dancers mid-motion behind the music trucks$vtg$, $vtg$The crowd-and-costume energy along the route$vtg$]::text[], $vtg${"wide":"A costumed masquerader filling the foreground, the parade trailing behind","normal":"Eye-level portraits of masqueraders who pose for you","tele":"Compress feathers and sequins into pure color, or a single face mid-dance","macro":"Costume craft — beadwork, feather detail, sequins in the light"}$vtg$::jsonb, $vtg$Route varies year to year — confirm before you go; typically central/SW Atlanta.$vtg$, $vtg$atlantacarnival.org$vtg$, true)
